problem_statement:
invalid: Variable "$var" is not defined
When executing a query in async-graphql, I'm getting a "Variable ... is not defined" error when I don't think I should be.

A query like

```graphql
query TestQuery($var: Boolean) {
    test(var: $var) {
        id
    }
}
```

with no variables

```json
{}
```

will return errors and no data.

```json
{
  "errors": [
    {
      "locations": [
        {
          "column": 15,
          "line": 2
        }
      ],
      "message": "Variable \"$var\" is not defined"
    }
  ]
}
```

However, according to [the GraphQL spec §6.1.2](http://spec.graphql.org/June2018/#sec-Coercing-Variable-Values), at instruction 3.g. it seems like this should be allowed.

A single example of a service that does allow this is [GitHub's API](https://developer.github.com/v4/explorer/), where

```graphql
query MyRepos($isFork:Boolean) { 
  viewer {
    repositories(first:10, isFork:$isFork) {
      nodes {
        name
      }
    }
  }
}
```

with no variables

```json
{}
```

returns data and no errors.

---

The exact reason I'm running into this is because I have a GraphQL server implemented in Juniper, and I'm converting it to async-graphql. My clients (using Apollo, but I'm not familiar with much more than that) are omitting certain variables at certain times. Juniper seems to allow this but async-graphql is returning errors.

